## Propagating Trace Context Across RabbitMQ

The issue is that RabbitMQ doesn't automatically propagate W3C trace context. You need to manually inject/extract it via message headers.

### Service A (Publisher) — Inject context into headers

```csharp
using System.Diagnostics;
using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;
using RabbitMQ.Client;

// Define an ActivitySource for your publisher
static readonly ActivitySource Source = new("ServiceA.Messaging");

// When publishing:
using var activity = Source.StartActivity("OrderEvent Publish", ActivityKind.Producer);

var props = channel.CreateBasicProperties();
props.Headers ??= new Dictionary<string, object>();

// Inject current trace context into message headers
if (activity != null)
{
    props.Headers["traceparent"] = activity.Id!;
    if (activity.TraceStateString is not null)
        props.Headers["tracestate"] = activity.TraceStateString;
}

channel.BasicPublish(exchange, routingKey, props, body);
```

### Service B (Consumer) — Extract context and link the trace

```csharp
using System.Diagnostics;

static readonly ActivitySource Source = new("ServiceB.Messaging");

// In your consumer callback:
var headers = ea.BasicProperties.Headers;

ActivityContext parentContext = default;
if (headers != null && headers.TryGetValue("traceparent", out var raw))
{
    var traceparent = System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetString((byte[])raw);
    ActivityContext.TryParse(traceparent, null, out parentContext);
}

using var activity = Source.StartActivity(
    "OrderEvent Process",
    ActivityKind.Consumer,
    parentContext);  // <-- links to publisher's trace
```

### Wire it up in `Program.cs` (both services)

```csharp
builder.Services.AddOpenTelemetry()
    .WithTracing(tracing => tracing
        .AddSource("ServiceA.Messaging")   // or ServiceB.Messaging
        .AddAspNetCoreInstrumentation()
        .AddOtlpExporter());
```

### Key points

1. **`traceparent`** is the W3C header that carries `trace-id` + `span-id` + flags.
2. RabbitMQ headers store values as `byte[]`, so decode with `Encoding.UTF8.GetString`.
3. Passing `parentContext` to `StartActivity` makes the consumer span a **child** of the producer span → end-to-end trace.
4. If you use MassTransit or NServiceBus, they do this automatically. The above is for raw `RabbitMQ.Client`.
